    "messages": [
      {
        "content": "In a car dealership with 600 cars, 60% of the cars are hybrids, and 40% of the hybrids contain only one headlight. How many of the hybrids have full headlights?",
        "role": "user"
      },
      {
        "content": "240",
        "role": "assistant"
      },
      {
        "content": "Given:\n- Total cars: 600\n- Percentage of hybrids: 60%\n- Percentage of hybrids with only one headlight: 40%\n\nFirst, calculate the number of hybrids:\n\\[ \\text{Number of hybrids} = 600 \\times 0.60 = 360 \\]\n\nNext, calculate the number of hybrids with only one headlight:\n\\[ \\text{Number of hybrids with one headlight} = 360 \\times 0.40 = 144 \\]\n\nTo find the number of hybrids with full headlights, subtract the number of hybrids with one headlight from the total number of hybrids:\n\\[ \\text{Number of hybrids with full headlights} = 360 - 144 = 216 \\]\n\nCHECK: The result (216) makes sense because it is less than the total number of hybrids (360) and greater than zero. It also aligns with the given percentages.\n\nFINAL: 216",
        "role": "assistant"
      },
      {
        "content": "Write your own reusable record: explain the specific operations, when they apply, and a concrete check using this problem. Retain its final answer. Solve in your own first-person voice, using 150–400 tokens. Identify the given quantities and requested unknown, explain the actual reusable operations connecting them, and check the result against the problem. Do not pad with generic advice or invent observations. Finish with a separate line FINAL: followed by just the numeric answer.",
        "role": "user"
      }
    ],
